            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0595" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24546/40: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nouméa</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVitty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nouméa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-01T22:00:00+11:00">December 1,
                            1941—10 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 2—4:06 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Department’s 25, November 29, [<hi rendition="#italic">27</hi>] 11 p.m. High
                    Commissioner today told me that he awaits confirmation that agreement has been
                    concluded between War Department and Free French delegation at Washington
                    concerning construction and utilization of air bases in New Caledonia. Until
                    this information is received he has instructions not to permit any new work on
                    bases to be undertaken by either the Australians or Americans. He requests that
                    the Hawaiian Department be notified that before taking any action as to sending
                    equipment or personnel he be informed through me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVitty</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
